() Tj T*
(6. Push to `main` or manually run the Pages workflow.) Tj T*
(7. Open `/web/admin.html` and sign in with the Supabase admin user.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Supabase anon key is designed to be exposed in a browser. Never put the Supabase) Tj T*
(service-role key in GitHub Pages, JavaScript, or the repository. The SQL policies are the) Tj T*
(security boundary.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The current client showcase in `app.js` is retained as a local fallback for design preview,) Tj T*
(while `public-data.js` reads published client profiles from Supabase in production.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Changeable public site details) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After running the updated `supabase-schema.sql`, sign in at `/web/admin.html`. The **Public) Tj T*
(site settings** panel lets an authenticated administrator change:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  • Contact email) Tj T*
(  • Contact number) Tj T*
(  • Head office) Tj T*
(  • Top announcement) Tj T*
(  • Essential plan price) Tj T*
(  • Partner plan price) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Changes are stored in Supabase and read by the public website. Do not edit these values in) Tj T*
(the browser developer tools; use the authenticated admin portal so the database remains the) Tj T*
(source of truth.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Video and document libraries) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Run `supabase-media-extension.sql` in Supabase SQL Editor to create:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  • `video_library` for YouTube videos) Tj T*
(  • `resource_library` for Google Docs and other Google document links) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(From the admin portal, choose **YouTube video** or **Google document link** in the content) Tj T*
(type selector. Enter a title, a dynamic category, the YouTube/Google URL and a description.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Published videos appear in the public video library with YouTube key-frame thumbnails and) Tj T*
(play links. Categories become filter buttons automatically. Published documents appear in) Tj T*
(the resource library and open in a new tab.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Website enquiries) Tj T*
